From 76b201fe515f450cda1b665648bbcdf58af7cfb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:33:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 115/116] dynarmic: A64 gets A32's offset folding, redundant
 extension skipping and cold code

fold_address_offsets, skip_redundant_extensions, split_cold_code for the A64 JIT. Folding with
fastmem's range check (unmirrored, under 64 bits): the base is compared with the arena's size
less the constant, so base + constant stays in the arena; past it the range check calls the
same stub a fault does (the fallback's stack alignment), with the address made whole in 64 bits
(A32 still wraps at 32). Cold code reserves at least 16 KiB a block. 128-bit accesses aren't
folded. Also per-core counts of the accesses fastmem was declined for (walked from then on).

Tests (harness, old build vs new with the options on): A64 gen5/gen6/gen8 x no fastmem, an
arena every access is past, a mapped arena, monitor exclusives, no shared walk: 1,500
programs the same; the code cache suites (save, reload, twice) with them; game.c built for
AArch64: the same result, 0.9% fewer instructions and 6% fewer I1 misses a frame (callgrind).
A32 against 04.20's build: 600 programs the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
