+    /// (PS4 04.22, as A32's) With fastmem, not mirrored: a load or store at a base register plus
+    /// a constant (LDR x0, [x1, #8]) takes the constant in its displacement ([r13 + base + 8])
+    /// instead of an add before it. The range check compares the base with the arena's size less
+    /// the constant, so the access stays in the arena; past it, the fallback gets the address whole.
+    bool fold_address_offsets = false;
+
+    /// (PS4 04.22, as A32's) A byte or halfword loaded (LDRB, LDRH) isn't zero-extended again (the
+    /// load did), and one stored from a register (STRB, STRH) is stored from it without a movzx
+    /// into another first.
+    bool skip_redundant_extensions = false;
+
+    /// (PS4 04.22, as A32's) A block's rarely run code (fault and slow-path stubs, float special
